# Cargo.lock IS committed here, deliberately.
# The published Monty interpreter reaches `ruff_python_ast 0.0.3`, which derives from
# `get-size2` while depending on an older `compact_str`; past `get-size2 0.10.0` the two
# disagree and it fails to compile. The manifest caps the version, and the lockfile is
# what makes that resolution reproducible rather than re-derived per machine. Remove both
# when the upstream mismatch is fixed.

target/

# Don't check in the local rustup toolchain override.
/rust-toolchain.toml

# don't check in local env config
.cargo/

# Local editor config
.vscode/

# macOS Finder metadata
.DS_Store

# .attach_pid{n} pop up frequently
# if you have older (<17) JDK versions in your dependency closure
# and generally should not be commited to git
# ref: https://bugs.openjdk.java.net/browse/JDK-8214300
.attach_*

# Local Claude Code agent and workflow definitions
.claude/agents/
.claude/workflows/
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# Python bytecode from test fixtures.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Research notes (`.exp.md`) and their generated index. The corpus is agent working
# material, so it stays local instead of shipping with the code.
/.agents/explorations/

# Proof-of-concept and throwaway code, one directory per POC. The tree is outside the
# Cargo workspace, so a normal build never compiles it. Its lockfiles, its compiled
# probes, and its sources all stay local with it.
/.agents/pocs/

# Draft decisions and specs from the `kd` and `spec` skills. Both are local working material: a
# decided decision is appended to `docs/design/decisions.md`, and a spec is never committed.
/.agents/drafts/

# Local scratch. Durable research belongs in .agents/explorations/ instead. An
# exploration that cites a clone under here records the commit it read.
/.tmp/

# Source binaries built for POCs.
#
# **Anchored, because a bare `sources/` matches that directory name at ANY depth.** It silently
# ignored `crates/credentials/src/sources/`, which is a tracked Rust module: the files
# already committed were unaffected, but every NEW file added there vanished from `git status` and
# from any commit. Measured — a new credential source went missing that way.
/pocs/**/sources/

# Spec task trackers. A `*.tasks.json` is per-effort execution state, so it stays local with the
# spec it tracks.
*.tasks.json

# Probe reports from a workload-suite run. Generated per run and uploaded as a
# GitHub artifact, so they stay local. Anchored, to match only this one dir.
/test-workload/run-reports/
